David worked at St. Mary's Hospital, a bustling facility known for its excellent patient care. Every morning, he would arrive at the hospital well before the sun rose, donning his crisp white uniform and a smile that never seemed to fade. His first task was to ensure that the patient rooms were spotless, from the gleaming floors to the neatly made beds. He took great care in arranging the linens, towels, and medical equipment with military-like precision.

David's dedication to order extended beyond the physical appearance of the rooms. He meticulously organized patient files, making sure that every chart was up to date and easily accessible for the medical staff. He knew that a well-organized system was crucial for efficient patient care, and he took his role in facilitating that seriously.

But David's orderly nature wasn't limited to his work at the hospital. His personal life was a testament to his love for structure. His apartment was a sanctuary of<|im_end|>

